<title>INDIA: Indian bullion markets closed for Christmas.</title>
<headline>Indian bullion markets closed for Christmas.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bombay bullion market was closed for Christmas on Wednesday. It will reopen on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, gold and silver held modest gains helped by an overnight uptrend in the world market. Standard gold rose 15 rupees to 5,030 per 10 grammes. Silver also gained 15 rupees to 6,920 rupees per kg. (Conversion $1=35.80 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22 265 9000</p>
</text>
